## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate edge ML costs into a robust business case, including privacy constraints, rollout risk, and financial metrics.

## Key Concepts
- On-device RL inference energy and latency
- Policy delta encoding and secure transmission
- Drift/maintenance costs and OTA rollout
- Privacy/compliance and data minimization
- Rollout strategy and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-cost estimator
function estimateCost(params) {
  const {
    dispatchesPerHour, energyPerDispatch, latencyMs,
    cloudSavingsPerDispatch
  } = params;
  // simplified calculation
  return energyPerDispatch * dispatchesPerHour / 3600;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate model drift in production and trigger rollback?
- What would you put in the go/no-go criteria to scale beyond pilot?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a cost-benefit for privacy-preserving identity with ZK; evaluates crypto choices, on-device constraints, privacy, compliance, rollout, and measurement plans.

## Key Concepts

- Zero-knowledge proofs (ZK)
- On-device cryptography and secure enclaves
- Energy/perf trade-offs in mobile environments
- Data minimization and regulatory compliance
- Rollout strategy and success metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo API for per-proof cost estimation
function estimateProofCost(securityLevel, proofSizeKB) {
  const cpuPerBit = securityLevel >= 128 ? 2 : 1;
  const energyPerOp = securityLevel >= 128 ? 0.5 : 0.2;
  return { cpuOps: proofSizeKB * 1000 * cpuPerBit, energyJ: proofSizeKB * 0.01 * energyPerOp };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the security of the ZK protocol chosen?
- How would you handle offline onboarding if network is unavailable?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to quantify edge privacy investments, regulatory costs, and business impact for a real-world data minimization feature across Cloudflare/Snowflake contexts.

## Key Concepts
- Edge data minimization and on-device processing
- Local aggregation and secure delta encoding
- Regulatory risk, data residency, and cost-of-change trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function deltaEncode(events) {
  // Simplified delta-encoding by event type counts
  const counts = {};
  for (const e of events) {
    counts[e.type] = (counts[e.type] || 0) + 1;
  }
  return counts;
}
```

